{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786429088,"nonce":"Mrt+UrfayxjAxLmCPX1R0WIhqOY=","message":"Done. 10 files, 168 test functions. No real sleeps; timeouts use expired deadlines and 1ns budgets.\n\nTHE ISSUE'S PREMISES WERE WRONG IN THREE PLACES:\n- There are FOUR enrichers, not five. silencematch/ contains only doc.go — no implementation, no registration, no reference anywhere in the tree. It is untestable because it does not exist.\n- domain/ was already tested (enrichment_test.go, 804 lines, 9b88a50), including Validate() thoroughly.\n- runbook never fetches a URL, by design — pinned by a test that points every annotation at a live httptest server with a hit counter and asserts zero hits.\n\nThe load-bearing assertion passes: three enrichers that error, panic and blow the budget, and NotifyPreNotificationReady is still called exactly once with the right arguments. Every failure path degrades to an explicit not-available — a zero Result and a mandatory Error, never a half-filled payload — with one correct exception, an enricher that returns StatusPartial itself.\n\nValidate() verdict: the type-level criticism is real (exported fields, no constructor, a zero value violating six CHECKs) and already recorded as TestBUG_EnrichmentIsConstructibleWhileInvalid. But 'a caller can store an invalid Enrichment' is FALSE — UpsertMany is the only write path to the table and validates every element before queueing a statement. Pinned from both sides, including that one bad row refuses the whole batch so a phase never lands half-written.\n\nFOUR DEFECTS FOUND IN runbook.link, all pinned as TestBUG_*, production untouched:\n1. An unresolved org-template placeholder ships as the Slack runbook BUTTON — expand()'s own doc says an unfilled {label} is rejected, but IsAbsoluteHTTPURL accepts {} in a path and url.String() percent-encodes it. Exactly the failure class this issue names: not a missing field, a field that looks populated and is wrong.\n2. normalise() uses the alert_sources.base_url predicate on operator links, so it refuses a query string, a fragment and a trailing slash — while the comment above it claims the opposite. A Grafana link with ?from=now-1h loses its button.\n3. A rejected link reports StatusSkipped ('Applicable said no') rather than partial, so a run that looked and found a broken annotation is filed identically to one that never ran.\n4. An uppercase scheme (HTTPS://) is rejected outright — looksLikeURL is case-sensitive and HTTPURLRe has no (?i), while normalise's ToLower(scheme) is a no-op twice over. RFC 3986 §3.1 makes schemes case-insensitive.\n\nNot covered: enrichment/worker, enrichment/api, and repository/alertread.go (being edited concurrently).","files":null}]}